				<div class="story-grid">
					<div class="story-narrative">
						<p>
							I started out fascinated by 3D animation, cinema, and digital cinematography—captivated by how light and motion evoke raw emotion. But as I worked on complex scenes, I realized my real passion wasn't just manipulating DCC tools: <strong>it was understanding exactly what happens under the viewport hood</strong>.
						</p>
						<p>
							How does the GPU schedule wavefronts? How can we march rays through mathematical Signed Distance Fields without polygon meshes? How do we pack data into GPU cache lines so that frame times stay under 11ms on mobile silicon?
						</p>
						<p>
							My engineering degree at <strong>Politecnico di Torino</strong> gave me a rigorous foundation in linear algebra, vector calculus, signal processing, and C++ systems programming. Since then, I’ve dedicated my work to operating at the razor-thin intersection between <strong>technical art and graphics programming</strong>.
						</p>
						<p>
							Whether building custom OpenGL rendering engines from scratch, authoring bio-adaptive volumetric compute shaders for Meta Quest 3, or scripting production add-ons in Blender, my goal is always the same: <strong>give artists limitless creative power while keeping the runtime blazing fast</strong>.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div class="philosophy-cards">
						<div class="philosophy-card">
							<div class="philosophy-title">
								<span>⚡</span>
